From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 12:46:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 48/48] Taskbar: the preview follows its item instead of
 closing

When a title changed the length of the hovered item or of one before
it (a terminal or browser title, tab counts, media, the clock), the
hover preview closed. The item under the resting pointer still counted
as hovered, so the preview only came back when the pointer crossed an
item edge, sometimes on the neighbour: it seemed to vanish and return.

Now the preview moves with its item: the popup's anchor is shifted by
the change in the lengths before it and of the item itself. It still
closes when the window has no item any more, moves between the panel
and the overflow list, or changes index (item widgets are keyed by
index, so another window's item is then under the pointer).

The applet logs one info line per preview open, reposition and close,
with the reason (hover, relayout, toplevel, leave, item-gone,
popup-done, ...) and the item index, to match future reports.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

